count           count.co2
  equation      "1 + 2 = 3" under NAT-DEC → ACCEPT — unconditional theorem relative to registered axiom set PEANO-ADD, Γ = ∅  (tests/accept/T7_one_plus_two.rlt)
  convention    NAT-DEC (interpretation input; executable: elaborator nat-dec, pinned) — explanation: "A run of decimal digits n denotes the numeral S^n(0). + denotes addition on the natural numbers and groups to the left: a + b + c reads (a + b) + c. = denotes equality on the natural numbers. Parentheses group."
  binding       1 ↦ {co2.c} · 2 ↦ {co2.o-1, co2.o-2}
  identities    co2.c, co2.o-1, co2.o-2 — 3 distinct reading point(s); class atom
  scope         particular (the reading points listed)
  association   a specification record: the kernel checked the equation; this file states what each numeral counts
  record valid (the kernel verdict above stands on its own)
